{"duration_api_ms":148120,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"c6f7766b-a47e-43bb-81ed-1c3956c65ad7","total_cost_usd":0.4536548,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":63542,"cache_read_input_tokens":60774,"output_tokens":15162,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7344},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":63542,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3908,"cache_read_input_tokens":56452,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11412,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11412},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":35644,"outputTokens":12,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.035704,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":15162,"cacheReadInputTokens":60774,"cacheCreationInputTokens":63542,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4179508,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":7344,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"req-1-lanb-zone\",\"requirement\":\"Bring node1's lan-b-facing interface (vtnet2) into service as its own zone with an address on lan-b\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"config.xml was edited to add a 'lanb' interface bound to vtnet2 with static IP 10.60.60.1/24 and description LANB; `configctl interface reconfigure lanb` returned OK and ifconfig confirmed vtnet2 UP with inet 10.60.60.1/24; `configctl filter reload` returned OK and pfctl -s rules shows a pass-in-quick rule scoped to the vtnet2 network plus a block rule anchoring the new zone, and pfctl -s nat shows outbound NAT covering vtnet2->vtnet0.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-43325d8c1234471b\",\"cmd-9432f18747b349ec\",\"cmd-91de030881634621\",\"cmd-77cf9e04e4774877\",\"cmd-21b487eb347b4677\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2-node3-reaches-node1-lanb\",\"requirement\":\"node3 reaches node1 on lan-b\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node3's enp8s0 (the NIC wired to lan-b per the nics topology) was persistently configured to 10.60.60.12/24 via nmcli, and a subsequent ping from node3 to node1's lanb address 10.60.60.1 succeeded with 0% loss.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-149f3e1f9cf94327\",\"cmd-090baa37a7cb48f4\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3-node3-reaches-node2-via-lana-through-node1\",\"requirement\":\"node3 reaches node2 on lan-a through node1\",\"status\":\"not_satisfied\",\"summary\":\"The authored topology assigns node1 three NICs (mgmt/vtnet0, lan-a/vtnet1, lan-b/vtnet2) and node2 two NICs (mgmt/enp1s0 DHCP, lan-a/enp8s0 static). node1's config.xml only ever contained the pre-existing 'lan' interface on vtnet0 (DHCP, 10.100.217.10) plus the newly added 'lanb'; vtnet1 (lan-a) was left fully unconfigured throughout (confirmed unconfigured both before and after the change, e.g. cmd-ab142efccb84457a). node2's lan-a NIC (enp8s0) was likewise never given a persistent address — the executor's own probe/revert sequence (cmd-000f7197070144ed, then reverted by cmd-47c7c7f014eb4952) shows enp8s0 ended with no IPv4 address. The 'node2 reachability' evidence the executor cites (cmd-090baa37a7cb48f4, cmd-989760d59fad42f8) pings node2's mgmt-network DHCP address 10.100.217.11 over enp1s0, which sits on the same flat 10.100.217.0/24 segment as node1's vtnet0 and node3's own enp1s0 — a path that does not require any lan-a zone or routing through node1's lanb interface. No lan-a addressing, route, or NAT/pass rule tied to lan-a was ever established, so the specific instructed outcome (reaching node2 via lan-a, routed through node1) is not demonstrated; the observed ping success is explained by pre-existing mgmt-network adjacency instead.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-5d4d4f39143141f2\",\"cmd-ab142efccb84457a\",\"cmd-000f7197070144ed\",\"cmd-47c7c7f014eb4952\",\"cmd-090baa37a7cb48f4\",\"cmd-5928fe5be66246a4\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4-ssh-preserved\",\"requirement\":\"Existing SSH management path on node1 preserved while applying the filter/interface changes\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"configctl filter reload returned OK and subsequent exec commands over the same SSH session succeeded; pfctl -s rules still shows the vtnet0 SSH pass rule intact after the change.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-91de030881634621\",\"cmd-77cf9e04e4774877\"]},{\"id\":\"req-5-node1-restart-evidence\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart protocol on node1: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered config/connectivity\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline kern.boottime captured (17:18:37); reboot issued and acknowledged; after a bounded series of timeouts, kern.boottime changed to 17:22:53 confirming a real reboot; post-restart check shows vtnet2/lanb and its pf pass rule intact, consistent with the fixed after_executor lifecycle snapshot's boot-identity of 17:22:53.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-f30d970b0f024d84\",\"cmd-f85505d86ab9469c\",\"cmd-1c775c8ff4224cd2\",\"cmd-1f1f442ba8144a85\"]},{\"id\":\"req-6-node2-restart-evidence\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart protocol on node2: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered connectivity\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 31949c21 captured with healthy enp1s0 address; reboot issued (ack ambiguous, stream closed, but plausible given subsequent timeouts); new boot_id 701be57e confirms reboot; enp1s0 address recovered and ping to node1 succeeded post-restart, consistent with the fixed after_executor snapshot boot_id.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-722ed685f13b46b0\",\"cmd-6f4c739826f34484\",\"cmd-c4f6169ace514396\",\"cmd-7e97f12ccb414443\"]},{\"id\":\"req-7-node3-restart-evidence\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart protocol on node3: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered lan-b config and connectivity\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 9feeb0bb captured; reboot issued (ack ambiguous stream closure, but followed by expected outage/timeouts); new boot_id 91d01ec7 confirms reboot; enp8s0's static 10.60.60.12/24 persisted and post-restart ping to node1 (lan-b) succeeded, consistent with the fixed after_executor snapshot boot_id. (The accompanying post-restart ping to node2 shares the same lan-a interpretation issue noted in req-3.)\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-ff82a2887c3840b5\",\"cmd-f4e09659e926442d\",\"cmd-58cd127c92a6454e\",\"cmd-989760d59fad42f8\"]}],\"confidence\":0.75,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.8,\"summary\":\"The executor ran a bounded topology-discovery sequence — temporarily assigning vtnet1/vtnet2 on node1 (cmd-2bb2c82f75af4978) and matching addresses on node2's enp8s0 (cmd-000f7197070144ed) and node3's enp8s0 (cmd-d2c16499cf1541e7) — to determine which physical NIC corresponded to lan-a vs lan-b via tcpdump; all three were promptly reverted (cmd-d0c74c1a6a9b414f, cmd-47c7c7f014eb4952, cmd-80d1f3ea12d6421a) and left no residue. This was a low-risk, fully-restored discovery step tied to a legitimate prerequisite (correctly identifying which vtnet maps to lan-b) so it is not treated as a serious violation. Several `configctl interface reload`/`configctl interface reload lanb` attempts failed with 'Action not allowed or